00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.170
Two things that
come to mind for me.

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:36.870
First of all, being
able to work in SQL.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.800
So something we found
in our Kaggle machine

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:40.800
learning developer survey
is that SQL's actually

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:43.623
the third most commonly used
language for machine learning.

00:07:43.623 --> 00:07:45.540
And also people who are
outside of the machine

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:48.090
learning AI space who are just
coming into it, many of them

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.400
are already familiar with SQL.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.858
So being able to use tools that
you already know how to use

00:07:51.858 --> 00:07:53.397
is a really big time saver.

00:07:53.397 --> 00:07:55.480
And also, you don't have
to download data locally.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:58.050
So if you've got sensitive data
that you can't store locally

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:00.690
or it's just like really big
and you can't store it on disk,

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:04.650
being able to do your
regression in BigQuery instead

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.210
of having to
download everything,

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.470
do your Python code and
then upload everything

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:11.012
once you've changed your model,
that can be a big time saver.

00:08:11.012 --> 00:08:12.428
SARA ROBINSON: And
to add to that,

00:08:12.428 --> 00:08:15.000
I think BQML is a great entry
point for machine learning.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.500
So you don't have to worry
about any sort of feature

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:17.035
engineering.

00:08:17.035 --> 00:08:18.910
So if you have categorical
data, for example,

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:20.430
if you're building
a model yourself,

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.150
you would have to one hot
encode that into arrays.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:25.620
BQML can recognize that
it's a categorical column

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:28.230
and transform your data for you.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.490
