So both BQML and AutoML make
it easy for anyone, regardless

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:47.820
of your machine
learning expertise,

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:49.820
to build your own custom
machine learning model.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:52.860
So you don't need a lot of
machine learning expertise

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:53.800
to get started.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.230
You just upload
your data, choose

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:57.960
the type of model you
want, and both BQML AutoML

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.327
will handle the rest.

00:08:59.327 --> 00:09:01.160
RACHAEL TATMAN: And
AutoML specifically, you

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:04.900
don't need as much
labeled data as well.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:08.120
So I know the natural
language API, sorry,

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.670
the natural language
AutoML that just launched,

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:13.980
you only need 100 label
examples per category

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.920
for each label in your
categorical learning

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:19.688
example, which is very little
data, especially when you're

00:09:19.688 --> 00:09:22.230
looking at like a BERT or ELMo,
these really, really enormous

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.670
GPT2, enormous language models.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:27.620
So being able to get started
with relatively little data,

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:30.470
smaller time investment, smaller
money investment for labeling

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:33.703
is a really big movement
towards democratization.

00:09:33.703 --> 00:09:34.620
STEPHANIE WONG: Great.

